UPDATE public.posts SET content='<p><strong>DTF prints South Africa</strong> has become the default choice for local brands, schools, sports clubs and event organisers who need vibrant, durable prints on almost any fabric without the setup costs of screen printing. This guide walks you through everything the Blank 2 Branded team has learned pressing tens of thousands of DTF transfers for South African customers — sizes, pricing in ZAR, fabrics, application, care and how to order.</p><img loading="lazy" src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1503342217505-b0a15ec3261c?w=1200&amp;q=80&amp;auto=format&amp;fit=crop" alt="DTF prints South Africa applied to a custom t-shirt"><h2>What DTF Printing Actually Is</h2><p>Direct-to-Film (DTF) is a print process where your artwork is printed onto a special PET film using pigment inks and hot-melt adhesive powder, then heat-pressed onto the garment. Unlike sublimation, DTF works on cotton, polyester, blends, canvas, nylon and even leather — light or dark. That flexibility is exactly why demand for <strong>DTF prints South Africa</strong> wide has exploded since 2023.</p><p>Compared with vinyl, DTF is softer, doesn''t crack the same way, and can reproduce full-colour photographic detail. Compared with screen printing, it wins on small runs — even a single tee is economical because there are no screens to burn. For a good international comparison, see the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://www.printful.com/blog/dtf-vs-dtg">Printful DTF vs DTG breakdown</a>.</p><h3>When DTF Is the Right Choice</h3><ul><li><p>Small to medium runs (1–500 units) where screens don''t pay off</p></li><li><p>Multi-colour or photographic designs that would need many screen colours</p></li><li><p>Mixed-fabric orders — cotton tees, poly hoodies and canvas bags in one job</p></li><li><p>Fast turnaround — most of our transfers ship within 24–48 hours</p></li></ul><h2>Sizes We Offer: A6 to 1 Meter</h2><p>For <strong>DTF prints South Africa</strong> buyers, we keep four standard sizes in stock so pricing stays predictable and quoting is instant:</p><ul><li><p><strong>A6 (105 × 148 mm)</strong> — pocket logos, sleeve prints, cap fronts</p></li><li><p><strong>A5 (148 × 210 mm)</strong> — left chest logos, small back prints</p></li><li><p><strong>A4 (210 × 297 mm)</strong> — standard front or back tee print</p></li><li><p><strong>1 Meter (roll)</strong> — bulk runs, oversized prints, gang sheets for resellers</p></li></ul><p>If you need a size in between, you can build a custom gang sheet on the product page — a huge cost-saver when you are pressing multiple designs from one meter of film.</p><h3>Typical ZAR Pricing in 2026</h3><p>Pricing varies with quantity, but as a rough guide: A6 from R15, A5 from R25, A4 from R45, and a full 1 m roll from R650. Volume tiers cut those numbers by 20–40%, and reseller accounts unlock roll pricing from your first order.</p><h2>The Application Process</h2><p>Applying a DTF transfer at home or in a workshop is quick once you have a heat press. Our standard operating procedure, after pressing more than 50 000 transfers for customers across South Africa, looks like this:</p><ol><li><p>Pre-press the garment for 5 seconds to remove moisture</p></li><li><p>Position the transfer, matte side up</p></li><li><p>Press at 150–160°C for 15 seconds at medium-firm pressure</p></li><li><p>Peel the film cold — wait 20–30 seconds before removing</p></li><li><p>Re-press through baking paper for 10 seconds to lock the finish</p></li></ol><p>Skipping the cold peel is the number-one mistake we see with new customers. It causes edge lifting after a few washes. A domestic iron can work in an emergency but you will not get the durability of a proper heat press with even pressure.</p><img loading="lazy" src="https://enpdahmqwhdukbnykqyy.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/blog-images/1784620040055-cki8ul.webp" alt="DTF Prints South Africa: The Complete 2026 Guide"><h3>Common Mistakes to Avoid</h3><ul><li><p>Pressing directly over seams or zips without a pressing pillow</p></li><li><p>Using low-quality baking paper that sticks to the finish</p></li><li><p>Washing the garment within 24 hours of pressing the transfer</p></li></ul><h2>Care and Longevity</h2><p>A well-pressed DTF transfer will comfortably survive 50+ wash cycles. We tell every customer buying <strong>DTF prints South Africa</strong> wide the same four care rules: wash cold, turn the garment inside out, tumble dry on low or line dry, and never iron directly over the print. We have seen team kits pressed in 2023 still looking sharp in 2026 because the crews followed those rules.</p><p>For a deeper technical breakdown of DTF ink chemistry and wash-fastness testing, the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://www.epson.com/direct-to-film-printing">Epson direct-to-film technical guide</a> is a solid reference.</p><p>One more note for buyers new to the process: DTF pigment inks are UV-stable, which matters in South Africa where summer sun in Gauteng, KZN and the Cape can fade cheaper prints within a season. Properly cured DTF holds its colour even on team kits worn outdoors every weekend, which is a big reason clubs and schools have shifted almost entirely away from vinyl in the last two years.</p><h2>Where to Buy DTF Prints in South Africa</h2><p>You have three practical options. Local walk-in print shops are fast but often limited to A4 and below. Online-only sellers are cheap but slow, with courier delays that hurt event deadlines. A hybrid supplier like Blank 2 Branded stocks blank apparel and prints in-house, so you get one invoice, one lead time and one point of contact when something needs a reprint.</p><p>For most SME brands, schools and clubs we work with, the hybrid model wins because reprints, colour matching and reruns are handled by the same team that pressed the first order — no finger-pointing between a print shop and an apparel wholesaler.</p><h3>What to Send Us</h3><ul><li><p>Print-ready artwork as PNG or PDF at 300 DPI with a transparent background</p></li><li><p>The size you want, or the garment we should size it against</p></li><li><p>Quantity per size — this drives your unit price</p></li></ul><h3>FAQ: DTF Prints South Africa</h3><p><strong>How long do DTF prints last on a t-shirt?</strong> A properly pressed and cured DTF transfer lasts 50 or more wash cycles when the garment is washed cold, turned inside out and tumble dried on low. In our workshop tests on 180 gsm cotton tees, prints still showed sharp edges and full colour after 60 washes over an eighteen-month period.</p><p><strong>Can I put DTF prints on dark or black shirts?</strong> Yes. DTF is one of the few print methods that reproduces bright colours and pure whites on black or navy garments without a separate under-base process, which is why so many South African teamwear brands have switched from screen printing to DTF for dark kits.</p><p><strong>Do you deliver DTF prints outside Gauteng?</strong> We courier DTF prints to every major metro in South Africa — Johannesburg, Pretoria, Cape Town, Durban, Gqeberha, East London, Bloemfontein, Polokwane and Mbombela — in two to four working days, with tracking on every parcel.</p><p><strong>What file format should I send for a DTF print?</strong> A transparent PNG at 300 DPI, sized to the print dimensions you need, works best. Vector PDFs or Adobe Illustrator files are also welcome and often reproduce edges more cleanly on small text.</p><p><strong>Is there a minimum order for DTF prints in South Africa?</strong> No. You can order a single A6 transfer if that is all you need. That said, gang-sheeting multiple designs onto a one-meter roll almost always brings your per-print cost down significantly, so most repeat customers move to roll orders within a few months.</p><h2>Ready to Order Your DTF Prints?</h2><p>At <strong>Blank 2 Branded</strong> we have been supplying <strong>DTF prints South Africa</strong> wide since 2022 from our Mbombela base, with courier to every major metro in 2–4 working days. Browse our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="/shop/products/dtf-print-a4">DTF prints range</a>, our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="/shop">blank apparel shop</a> or <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="/contact">contact our team</a> for a bulk quote.</p><p><em>Liked this guide? </em><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="/blog"><em>Read more on our blog</em></a><em> for practical guides on branding, apparel and custom prints in South Africa.</em></p>', updated_at=now() WHERE id='63020ec8-986f-4400-b0b4-9839815d5b78';